---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Guides" 
  description="In-depth guides on API mocking, test data generation, and testing best practices."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Guides</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Learn how to use API mocking and test data tools effectively in your projects.
    </p>
    
    <div class="guide-grid">
      <a href="/comparisons/msw-vs-nock-vs-polly/" class="guide-card">
        <span class="guide-badge">Comparison</span>
        <h2>MSW vs Nock vs Polly.js</h2>
        <p>Compare three popular JavaScript HTTP mocking libraries and find the right fit for your project.</p>
        <div class="guide-meta">
          <span>🛠️ Tools: MSW, Nock, Polly.js</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      
      <a href="/guides/openapi-mock-server-prism/" class="guide-card">
        <span class="guide-badge">Tutorial</span>
        <h2>Spec-First Mocking with Prism and OpenAPI</h2>
        <p>Generate mock servers directly from your OpenAPI specifications using Prism.</p>
        <div class="guide-meta">
          <span>🛠️ Tools: Prism</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      
      <a href="/guides/mock-api-react-native/" class="guide-card">
        <span class="guide-badge">Tutorial</span>
        <h2>Mocking APIs in React Native with Mockifyer</h2>
        <p>Record and replay HTTP interactions in React Native applications for reliable testing.</p>
        <div class="guide-meta">
          <span>🛠️ Tools: Mockifyer</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      
      <a href="/guides/faker-js-test-data-factories/" class="guide-card">
        <span class="guide-badge">Best Practices</span>
        <h2>Realistic Test Data with Faker and Factories</h2>
        <p>Create maintainable, realistic test data using Faker and factory patterns with Fishery.</p>
        <div class="guide-meta">
          <span>🛠️ Tools: Faker, Fishery</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      
      <a href="/guides/pact-contract-testing-javascript/" class="guide-card">
        <span class="guide-badge">Best Practices</span>
        <h2>Keeping Mocks Honest with Pact</h2>
        <p>Use consumer-driven contract testing to ensure your mocks stay in sync with real APIs.</p>
        <div class="guide-meta">
          <span>🛠️ Tools: Pact</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .subtitle {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  
  .guide-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(350px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  
  .guide-card {
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s;
    display: block;
  }
  
  .guide-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
  }
  
  .guide-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 12px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .guide-card h2 {
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .guide-card p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .guide-meta {
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .guide-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
